# Public document shapes

- Types for the UI belong next to the client (`AuthContext` `User`) or as Convex `returns` validators — not inline `any`.
- camelCase, matching `schema.ts` (`firstName`, `homeFacilityId`).
- Do not prefix types with `Convex` / `Directus` / `Prisma`. Use domain names: `User`, `Patient`, `AccessDecision`.
- Never send `hashedPassword`, session `token` hashes you do not need, or full clinical rows on search.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD
return user; // includes hashedPassword

// ✅ GOOD — convex/auth.ts publicUser
function publicUser(user: {
  _id: Id<"users">;
  email: string;
  roles: UserRole[];
  hospital: string;
  department?: string;
  accountStatus: "active" | "suspended";
  profile: { firstName: string; lastName: string; middleName?: string };
}) {
  return {
    _id: user._id,
    email: user.email,
    roles: user.roles,
    hospital: user.hospital,
    department: user.department,
    accountStatus: user.accountStatus,
    profile: user.profile,
  };
}
```

Search/discovery returns identity + record **existence**, not `clinicalSummaries`.
